WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:01.880
Let's see.

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:04.630
We're hearing from so many different people
here.

00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:08.370
Why don't we go to Skylar from New York, Skylar
from New York.

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:09.650
You're on the air.

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:12.650
Hey, David, can you hear me?

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:13.650
Yes, I can.

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:14.650
Awesome.

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:18.230
So I was wondering, obviously, for the better
part of a year we've been talking about, let's

00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:22.779
just get the ball back, let's just have a
win and then we can push them.

00:00:22.779 --> 00:00:27.060
How do we make the next four years productive
in that we're not just comparing everything

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:32.059
Biden does to what Trump did, but to actually
push them back and pressure him and educate

00:00:32.059 --> 00:00:35.070
people to vote in more of their best interests?

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:40.170
Well, the first step, as we have to compare
Biden to his campaign promises, and you're

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:45.580
absolutely right, that if we simply say this
is how it compares to Trump, everything will

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:46.900
essentially be better.

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:52.560
Maybe we'll stumble across something where
we say, wow, Biden somehow is even worse than

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:53.920
Trump on this one issue.

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:57.040
I think those issues will be few and far between,
if any.

00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:04.030
But I think the first step is we as progressive
media have to remind the audience not just

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:07.280
about what Trump would have done, but what
did Biden promise.

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:08.280
That's the start.

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:11.780
And if we forget that, then we don't stand
a chance.

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:17.740
And then beyond that, obviously, with the
midterms and hopefully growing influence for

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:24.210
the Progressive Caucus in the House of Representatives,
there will be continued pressure on Joe Biden.

00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:27.979
But the most important thing is let's keep
let's hold Joe Biden accountable to his own

00:01:27.979 --> 00:01:29.069
promises.

00:01:29.069 --> 00:01:33.530
Yeah, because like I've already seen when
it comes to, like, people he's named in his

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:37.850
cabinet or the way that he's gone about just
like trying to work with Republicans, that

00:01:37.850 --> 00:01:41.139
he's already getting a lot of pushback from
the left.

00:01:41.139 --> 00:01:44.810
And then I'm also seeing my guys, whether
it actually be president for a week before

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:46.049
we start criticizing him.

00:01:46.049 --> 00:01:47.049
Yeah.

00:01:47.049 --> 00:01:53.029
And on working with Republicans, I think all
there is so far to criticize is what is there

00:01:53.029 --> 00:01:54.029
to criticize.

00:01:54.029 --> 00:01:57.990
Biden has said he wants unity and he looks
forward to making progress with his friends

00:01:57.990 --> 00:02:02.850
across the aisle, like he likes to say there's
nothing wrong with him saying that it's naive

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:07.329
if he thinks he's going to do it because they're
not going to they will be obstructionist clowns.

00:02:07.329 --> 00:02:10.720
But I think it's silly to criticize Biden
for saying it.

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:15.780
I think what Biden would be wrong to do is
to think that he'll be able to negotiate with

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:17.720
these people when they when he won't.

00:02:17.720 --> 00:02:21.510
But so far, I don't I don't think there's
any criticism that would be levied just for

00:02:21.510 --> 00:02:23.450
Biden saying he's going to try it.

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:27.060
I think it's great to say let's try to work
together and get things done as long as he

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:30.510
doesn't end up compromising on what he campaigned
on.

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:35.030
Yeah, I just don't know the most productive
way to raise the bar, because if you look

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:39.390
at the Obama administration, it's easy to
compare it to George W. Bush and say Obama

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:40.580
did a tremendous job.

00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:44.550
But obviously, if that was the case, it wouldn't
have led to the election of Trump.

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:45.960
Well, that's why I think it's.

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:52.180
Remember, on paper, Biden's campaign platform
is well to the left of Obama's.

00:02:52.180 --> 00:02:58.260
I would argue that Joe Biden's platform and
his campaign promises are the most progressive

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:01.090
of any president that has become president.

00:03:01.090 --> 00:03:03.120
Now we have to hold him to them.

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:09.780
If we do if Biden does the stuff he promised,
then we're going to be moving the Overton

00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:10.790
Window left.

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:16.250
If Biden comes back from his promises and
just operates as a centrist, then we're going

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:17.870
to be extraordinarily disappointed.

00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:18.870
Absolutely.

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:24.930
Yeah, so I guess, you know, all we could do
at this point is wait and see and make our

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:26.980
voices heard in the most productive way possible.

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:27.980
Absolutely.

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:30.540
And make your voices heard through your local
representatives.

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:35.050
I mean, your members of the House and Senate
that represent where you live.

00:03:35.050 --> 00:03:40.290
Yeah, well, thankfully, my representative
is and Kathleen Rice, so I had a lot of work

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:41.290
to do.

00:03:41.290 --> 00:03:42.290
OK, yeah, that's an uphill battle.

00:03:42.290 --> 00:03:43.290
All right.

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:45.910
All right, my friend, thank you so much.

